{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Pre-flight Quality Check",
  "description": "Before any shell command that runs a noiseless or noisy pipeline experiment, runs the VQE quality predictor to warn if the configuration is likely to fail. Prevents wasting compute on doomed runs.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preToolUse",
    "toolTypes": [
      "shell"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "If the shell command being executed contains 'run_noiseless_pipeline' or 'run_thesis_variants' or 'run_scaling_validation', extract the --topology, --n-qubits, --p-layers, and --model arguments from the command. Then run a quick quality prediction: from qmbp_simulation.analysis.quality_predictor import QualityPredictor; p = QualityPredictor(); r = p.predict(...). If the prediction is ABORT, warn the user that this config is historically unlikely to succeed and suggest alternatives. If PROCEED or CAUTION, respond with '✅ Quality check passed (probability: X%)'. If the command is NOT a pipeline run, respond '✅ Not a pipeline experiment'."
  }
}